# Manual requests for the API. Run them in order with "Send Request" (Visual Studio,
# Rider, or VS Code with the REST Client extension). Start the API with the "http"
# launch profile, and apply migrations once first: dotnet ef database update
#
# /v1/auth/ endpoints allow 10 requests per minute per IP (specs/07-nfr.md).
#
# The refresh token is only ever in the refresh_token cookie (ADR 0013): copy its value from the
# Set-Cookie header of the login (or refresh) response into @refreshToken below. The requests send it
# explicitly, because clients differ in keeping cookies, and some drop a Secure cookie over plain http.

@BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5107
@email = ann@example.test
@password = correct horse battery
@refreshToken = paste-the-refresh_token-cookie-value-here

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### Sign up (409 EmailTaken if already done; then just log in)
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ann Example",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "timeZone": "Europe/London"
}

### Log in: the access token is captured for the requests below; copy refresh_token from Set-Cookie into @refreshToken
# @name login
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Profile and roles
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Change name or time zone (send only what changes)
PATCH {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timeZone": "America/New_York"
}

### Refresh: rotates the refresh token; the new one is in Set-Cookie (send the same token twice to see
### reuse detection: 401 InvalidRefreshToken, which also clears the cookie)
# @name refresh
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/refresh
Cookie: refresh_token={{refreshToken}}

### Profile with the refreshed access token
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.accessToken}}

### Log out: revokes every refresh token from this login and clears the cookie (204); paste the newest token first
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/logout
Cookie: refresh_token={{refreshToken}}

### Admin creates an owner and their business (T6). The logged-in user must be an admin first:
###   dotnet src/BookingPlatform.Api/bin/Debug/net10.0/BookingPlatform.Api.dll admin grant <email> [--granted-by <admin email>]
### (run with ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development). 201 with Location; a second run gives 409 AlreadyOwner.
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/admin/owners
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerName": "Olive Owner",
  "ownerEmail": "olive@example.test",
  "businessName": "Cut & Dry",
  "businessTimeZone": "America/New_York"
}

### Resend an invite (T7): an admin for an owner, or an owner for their staff. 204; 422 InviteNotPending
### once the account has a password; 404 for anyone else. Put the invited user's ID here (GET /v1/me as them,
### or SELECT id FROM users WHERE email = 'olive@example.test').
@invitedUserId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/users/{{invitedUserId}}/resend-invite
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Accept an invite (T7). Until the worker sends emails (T26), make a token by hand: pick any random
### string as the token and store its lowercase hex SHA-256 on the user's newest invite, e.g. in MySQL:
###   UPDATE user_invites SET token_hash = SHA2('my-test-token', 256), expires_at = UTC_TIMESTAMP() + INTERVAL 7 DAY
###   WHERE id = '<newest invite id>';
### 200 with tokens, then 400 InviteInvalid if sent again.
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/accept-invite
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "my-test-token",
  "password": "a new password for olive"
}

### Request a password recovery email (T7a). Always 202 with no body, whether or not the account exists;
### within 5 minutes of the last request for the account nothing new is stored. Until the worker sends emails
### (T26), find the row with SELECT * FROM password_resets ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 1.
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### Set a new password from a recovery link (T7a). Make a token by hand, as for invites:
###   UPDATE password_resets SET token_hash = SHA2('my-reset-token', 256), expires_at = UTC_TIMESTAMP() + INTERVAL 1 HOUR
###   WHERE id = '<newest password_resets id>';
### 200 with tokens (every other session is revoked), then 400 ResetLinkInvalid if sent again.
### This sets the password to "{{password}}" again, so the requests above keep working.
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "my-reset-token",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Change the password while logged in (T7a): 200 with new tokens, and every other session is revoked;
### 422 CurrentPasswordIncorrect for a wrong current password. The new password here equals the current one
### (allowed), so the requests above keep working. Log in again first if the access token has expired (15 minutes).
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "{{password}}"
}

### A business and its settings (T8): any signed-in user. Put a business ID here (the "id" from creating an
### owner above, ownedBusinessId in GET /v1/me as the owner, or SELECT id FROM businesses).
@businessId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Change the business's name or settings (T8): owner only, 403 for anyone else. As written this uses the
### {{email}} login above, so set @email and @password to the owner's (e.g. olive@example.test with the password
### set through accept-invite) and send the login request again first. Send only what changes.
### Limits: minNoticeMinutes 0-525600, cancellationWindowHours 0-8760, maxAdvanceDays 1-3650, slotStepMinutes 1-1440.
PATCH {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "minNoticeMinutes": 60,
  "slotStepMinutes": 15
}

### Services of a business (T9): any signed-in user. Ordered by name, then id; pages of ?limit= (1-200,
### default 50). Pass a page's nextCursor as ?cursor= for the next page; nextCursor is null on the last page.
# @name services
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/services?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Create a service (T9): owner only, logged in as above. Price is a string, returned with two decimals.
### durationMinutes 1-1440, buffers 0-1440, price at most 99999999.99; description optional (blank = none).
# @name createService
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "description": "Wash, cut and dry",
  "durationMinutes": 60,
  "bufferBeforeMinutes": 10,
  "bufferAfterMinutes": 5,
  "price": "45"
}

### A service and its assigned staff (T9): any signed-in user
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/services/{{createService.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Change a service (T9): owner only; send only what changes, "description": null clears it.
### Existing bookings keep their duration and buffers (ADR 0004).
PATCH {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/services/{{createService.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": "50",
  "description": null
}

### Staff of a business (T10): any signed-in user; removed staff are not listed. By name, then staffId.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Add a staff member (T10): owner only. A new email gets an account without a password and an invite;
### an existing account is linked (the name is then ignored). Adding the owner's own email makes them staff
### (no email sent). Re-adding a removed member restores them. 409 AlreadyStaff if already staff.
# @name addStaff
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sam Staff",
  "email": "sam@example.test"
}

### Replace the services a staff member performs (T10): owner only. Every ID must be a service of the
### staff member's business; [] removes them all. Uses the service created above.
PUT {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{addStaff.response.body.staffId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceIds": ["{{createService.response.body.id}}"]
}

### Weekly availability (T11): the owner and the business's staff may view; staff set their own, the owner
### anyone's. Times are local HH:mm (00:00-23:59) in the business's time zone; blocks on a day can't overlap.
@staffId = {{addStaff.response.body.staffId}}
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/weekly-availability
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Replace the whole week (T11). An empty "blocks" list clears it.
PUT {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/weekly-availability
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blocks": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "Monday", "startLocal": "09:00", "endLocal": "12:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "Monday", "startLocal": "13:00", "endLocal": "17:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "Saturday", "startLocal": "10:00", "endLocal": "14:00" }
  ]
}

### Date exception (T11): different hours for one date ...
PUT {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/date-exceptions/2026-12-24
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ranges": [{ "startLocal": "09:00", "endLocal": "12:00" }]
}

### ... or none at all
PUT {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/date-exceptions/2026-12-25
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "unavailable": true
}

### List date exceptions (T11), one item per date; from and to are inclusive local dates
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/date-exceptions?from=2026-12-01&to=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Remove a date exception (T11): 204, or 404 if that date has none
DELETE {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/date-exceptions/2026-12-24
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Time off (T12): viewed like availability; staff block their own, the owner anyone's. Timestamps are UTC
### with a Z (no offsets). Entries may overlap and may be in the past. Ordered by start; from/to filter the start.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/time-off?from=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Block time off (T12, T18): endUtc is exclusive and after startUtc. If it overlaps bookings that have not ended
### (buffers included), the answer is 409 ConfirmationRequired listing them; send the same request again with
### "confirm": { "affectedBookingIds": [...] } to save it and cancel them (R6).
# @name timeOff
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/staff/{{staffId}}/time-off
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startUtc": "2026-12-24T09:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2026-12-24T17:00:00Z"
}

### Remove time off (T12): 204, or 404 if it doesn't exist (any more)
DELETE {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/time-off/{{timeOff.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Open slots (T13): any signed-in user. from/to are inclusive local dates in the business's time zone, at most
### 30 dates (else 400 RangeTooLong). Optional staffId; ignoreMinimumNotice=true is for the owner, or staff with
### their own staffId (else 403). Past and beyond-window dates simply give no slots.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/services/{{createService.response.body.id}}/slots?from=2026-12-01&to=2026-12-07
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Book a slot (T14): startUtc must be a start the slots query offers (else 422 SlotUnavailable). customerEmail
### books on behalf of that account, and overrideMinimumNotice bypasses R3; both are for the owner, or staff with
### their own staffId (else 403). A taken time is 409 SlotConflict naming only the requested slot (R7).
# @name createBooking
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{createService.response.body.id}}",
  "staffId": "<staffId from the slots response>",
  "startUtc": "2026-12-01T14:00:00Z"
}

### A booking (T16): its customer, its staff member or the owner; anyone else 404.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Its history (T16, ADR 0003), oldest first; actor.userId only for the staff member and the owner.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### My bookings as customer (T16). Optional status=Confirmed|Cancelled, from/to on the start (from inclusive, to exclusive), limit, cursor.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/me/bookings?status=Confirmed
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### A business's bookings (T16): the owner sees all (optional staffId); staff only their own (another staffId is 403); others 404.
GET {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Reschedule (T17, R5): same booking ID. Customers outside the window (R4) and with the same staff member only;
### staff to their own slots; the owner to any staff (staffId). The current staff and start is a 200 no-op.
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startUtc": "2026-12-01T15:00:00Z"
}

### Cancel (T17, R4): customers outside the window (exactly N hours before is allowed); staff and owners any time.
POST {{BookingPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/v1/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
